spec fp03-session-read-bounded-by-context: 2 sessions, 2 permutations
# FP03. s0 writes s and reserves its commit instant (the commit hold); s1 commits t1 through a cypher.Session (autocommit CREATE)
# and then waits for its own commit with a 50 ms deadline: the wait returns the context
# error instead of hanging (CLAUDE.md, context-aware blocking). After s0 publishes, the
# same wait returns at once. The control interleaving publishes s0 before s1 commits.

starting permutation: s0w s0a s1w s1r s0p s1r2
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s1w: <cypher.Session, deadline 30s> CREATE (n:N {name:'t1'}) RETURN n.name AS name
name
----
"t1"
(1 row)
step s1r: <cypher.Session, deadline 50ms> MATCH (n {name:'t1'}) RETURN n.name AS name
ERROR: deadline exceeded
step s0p: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1r2: <cypher.Session, deadline 30s> MATCH (n {name:'t1'}) RETURN n.name AS name
name
----
"t1"
(1 row)
final ffr: <MVCCStats: in_flight_commits, sessions_waiting>
in_flight_commits|sessions_waiting
-----------------+----------------
0                |0               
(1 row)
final final: <sessionless> MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name, n.v AS v ORDER BY name
name|v   
----+----
"s" |1   
"t1"|null
(2 rows)

